# Parity capture evidence (screenshots, frame dirs, motion videos) are
# large regenerable artifacts that bloat the repo and break GitHub's
# file-size limits. The durable record is the textual findings in
# docs/parity/*.md; raw captures stay local-only. The .pilgrim seed
# fixture (docs/parity/fixtures/) IS tracked — it's the test input.
docs/parity/evidence/

# Parity verification scaffolding is local working tooling, not a
# repo deliverable. The durable record is docs/parity/2026-05-15-parity-ledger.md
# (the parity truth artifact) + docs/parity/gate.md (the ship rule) +
# docs/parity/fixtures/ (the .pilgrim test input) — those stay tracked.
# Everything else (superseded intermediate audits, capture how-to,
# review-protocol scaffolding) is regenerable working scratch.
docs/parity/*-audit.md
docs/parity/*-audit-v2.md
docs/parity/*-triage.md
docs/parity/capture-recipe.md
docs/parity/review-protocol.md
docs/parity/README-parity-ledger.md
*.hprof
